    "result_text": "All 278 tests pass \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented rejection of owner creation when the owner's city already contains 8 owners, responding with HTTP 400.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **New exception** `service/CityOwnerLimitExceededException.java` \u2014 a `RuntimeException` following the existing `DailyOwnerRegistrationLimitExceededException` pattern.\n\n2. **`service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 added a `cityOwnerLimitReached(owner)` check in `saveOwner` (only for new owners, before persist) that throws the new exception when the owner's city already holds `MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY = 8` owners. City comparison reuses the existing `normalizeKey` helper, so it's case/whitespace-insensitive and consistent with the duplicate-detection logic. Updates to existing owners are exempt (guarded by `owner.isNew()`).\n\n3. **`rest/advice/ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` that maps the new exception to `400 Bad Request` (mirroring the daily-limit handler).\n\n**Tests:**\n\n- Added `createOwnerRejectedWhenCityAlreadyHasEightOwners` to `OwnerRestControllerV1Tests` \u2014 fills a fresh city with 8 owners (all 201), then asserts the 9th gets 400.\n- Updated the existing `createOwnerRejectedWhenDailyLimitReached` test: it created 20 owners all in \"Madison\", which now conflicts with the per-city cap. Since its intent is the *daily* limit, each of its 20 owners now uses a distinct city so the two limits stay isolated.\n\nThe seed data has only 4 Madison owners, so the other tests that create a Madison owner remain well under the cap.",
